# st-driver test environment
#
# The suite is LIVE: it talks to a running SillyTavern and launches a real
# browser. Always point it at the dedicated TEST instance, not the daily-driver
# one - the tests create/delete characters, chats, groups, worlds and personas
# (all __drvtest_-prefixed and cleaned up, but you do not want that churn on
# your real library).
#
# bash / Git Bash:
#   export ST_URL=http://localhost:8000
#   export ST_DATA_ROOT="C:/Users/zouyue/SillyTavern/test/SillyTavern/data/default-user"
#   npm test
#
# Windows cmd:
#   set ST_URL=http://localhost:8000
#   set ST_DATA_ROOT=C:\Users\zouyue\SillyTavern\test\SillyTavern\data\default-user
#   npm test

# Server under test (default http://localhost:8000)
ST_URL=http://localhost:8000

# The server's data/default-user directory. Enables filesystem-level assertions
# (folder auto-creation quirks, movingUI fixture sweep). Unset -> those checks
# skip gracefully; HTTP coverage is unaffected either way.
ST_DATA_ROOT=C:/Users/zouyue/SillyTavern/test/SillyTavern/data/default-user

# Browser executable for the UI track. Auto-detected (system Edge/Chrome) when unset.
# ST_BROWSER_PATH=

# Opt-in: run real-LLM generation tests (spends tokens on the configured backend).
# ST_DRIVER_LIVE_GEN=1

# Opt-in: run tests that make real outbound internet calls (search visit/transcript).
# ST_DRIVER_LIVE_NET=1
